1
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,199
(Episode 4)

2
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,960
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,480
That's impossible.

4
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,440
They gathered three of the most authoritative handwriting experts,

5
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:00,680
and they all say Shek Chung wrote it.

6
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,600
With such important evidence,

7
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,840
I can only try to use procedural grounds...

8
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,120
to persuade the judge not to admit it.

9
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,040
I'm absolutely sure this one is fake. The real one...

10
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,880
Experts? They can get lost!

11
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,800
We can also find experts to say it's fake.

12
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:19,960
It's just a matter of money.

13
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,720
But these three are the top authorities.

14
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,120
If we find others, they might not be as convincing.

15
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,440
I don't care.

16
00:02:26,441 --> 00:02:29,440
If they find 3, we can find 10 or 20.

17
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,160
Why aren't you going yet?

18
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:57,400
I know you took the original will.

19
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,080
I assume you have already destroyed it.

20
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:04,520
So you're admitting this one is a forgery.

21
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,440
No, this one was also written by Shek Chung.

22
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:10,280
Can't you even recognize his handwriting?

23
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,520
You paid someone to forge it.

24
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,680
Actually,

25
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,400
I have a fingerprint report too.

26
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,640
The draft will is covered in Shek Chung's fingerprints.

27
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,760
Shek Chung didn't want to leave the estate to you.

28
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,440
You made him come back from the dead just to write this.

29
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,240
Get out!

30
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,280
I will definitely prove this is fake.

31
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,440
I also found a letter.

32
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,080
Read it before you say anything else.

33
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,840
- They're coming. Mr. Shek! - Yes.

34
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,360
- They're coming out. - Mr. and Mrs. Shek are coming out.

35
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,760
Mr. Shek, can you give us a comment?

36
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,680
The court has admitted the draft will as evidence.

37
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,720
What are your thoughts?

38
00:04:53,721 --> 00:04:56,480
We're very grateful to the judge for handling this case fairly.

39
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,720
We're also grateful to my father-in-law's spirit...

40
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,880
for letting us find the key evidence in time.

41
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,320
Do you feel like victory is in your grasp?

42
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,440
I wouldn't go that far.

43
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,600
But we are very optimistic about the result.

44
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:08,000
We believe the truth is on our side.

45
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,680
My father will surely watch over us.

46
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,320
Do you two have anything else to add?

47
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,400
How are you feeling right now?

48
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,760
- Does Mr. Shek have any comments? - Just a few words.

49
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:17,520
- It's Mrs. Shek! - Mrs. Shek!

50
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,880
Mrs. Shek, please say something.

51
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:20,760
Do you feel the situation is looking grim?

52
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:25,000
- Say something. - Anything to add?

53
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,800
Please move aside. We're about to drive off.

54
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:30,720
- Look over here, Mrs. Shek! - Mrs. Shek, over here!

55
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,240
Edward.

56
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,400
- Mrs. Yeung. - Hello.

57
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:37,840
Why are you here?

58
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,680
I'm here to see how amazing my husband is.

59
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,040
Patrick and the others thought...

60
00:05:41,041 --> 00:05:43,080
your 100 percent undefeated record would be broken.

61
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,960
I said impossible, my husband would never lose.

62
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,840
By the way, Dad came back early.

63
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,120
He said he wants to talk to you.

64
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,840
I've booked a table at the Seasons.

65
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,200
But we have a meeting later.

66
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,080
I already promised Dad.

67
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:02,520
Okay, let's talk tonight then.

68
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,680
- Okay. - Bye.

69
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:17,320
Mr. Lee Cheuk Kei made a will in 2002,

70
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:21,640
stating that all his assets would be left to his wife,

71
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:25,080
the defendant in this case, Ms. Leung Ka Ling.

72
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,960
The core of this dispute...

73
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,160
is the authenticity of this will.

74
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,200
Handwriting experts from both sides have their own versions.

75
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:39,239
Furthermore, the defendant, Ms. Leung, has shown that...

76
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,960
the plaintiff, Mr. Lee Wai Tak's, attack...

77
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:43,760
on Mr. Lai Hoi Wai's testimony...

78
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:46,760
is based entirely on hypothetical and unfair inferences.

79
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,400
There is simply no sufficient evidence.

80
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,679
Yet, the judges of the Court of First Instance...

81
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,960
and the Court of Appeal...

82
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,520
both required the defendant, Ms. Leung Ka Ling,

83
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,400
to clarify all doubts in the testimony.

84
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,240
This fundamentally violates legal principles.

85
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:05,520
So I urge Your Honors to set things right...

86
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,440
and grant the defendant a fair trial,

87
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,520
returning to her, as a wife,

88
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,440
the deceased's intentions from eight years ago.

89
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,839
- Mr. Yeung is here! Mr. Yeung! - Mr. Yeung!

90
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:17,199
This inheritance dispute of the century...

91
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,200
has lasted eight years.

92
00:07:18,201 --> 00:07:19,360
From the Court of First Instance...

93
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,719
to the Court of Appeal, you lost both.

94
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,159
Now at the Court of Final Appeal, you finally turned the tables...

95
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,280
after taking over.

96
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,720
People say you can spot details that no one notices,

97
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,600
and they've nicknamed you the Hawkeye Barrister.

98
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,000
How do you feel right now?

99
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,319
This has definitely been...

100
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:34,040
the most challenging case of my career.

101
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,960
I'm glad the deceased's final wish can finally be fulfilled.

102
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,639
It's said the total legal fees for both sides...

103
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:39,679
exceed 100 million dollars.

104
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,240
That's a record-breaker. What's your take on that?

105
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,760
If you ask my client,

106
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:45,200
I'm sure she will think it was well worth it.

107
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,400
- Can you say more? - Goodbye.

108
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,280
I want to be your apprentice. Here is my resume.

109
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,640
I don't take apprentices.

110
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,520
I've studied all your cases.

111
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,040
I even analyzed this case.

112
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,440
I didn't expect you to use this angle to fight it.

113
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,960
Take a look first. You'll take me as your apprentice after reading it.

114
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,960
We're on the same side. Don't be afraid.

115
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,040
I saw the news and thought you looked familiar.

116
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,080
So you really are that rich lady's lawyer.

117
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,240
You just collected 100 million dollars in legal fees.

118
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,240
There's no reason to pay so little. We're so close.

119
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,040
The price is fixed. Are you selling or not?

120
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,240
I'll sell it if you give me another 10,000 dollars.

121
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,520
If you don't pay, I'll tell everyone.

122
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:18,480
That the Hawkeye Barrister is addicted to painkillers.

123
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:22,160
Try it and I'll sue you for defamation.

124
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,000
I can sue you until you're bankrupt.

125
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,440
Are you selling it or not?

126
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,400
No.

127
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:48,960
Come here.

128
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,240
You.

129
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,800
Don't leave.

130
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,920
Illegal possession of unregistered pharmaceutical products.

131
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,880
A maximum fine of 100,000 dollars and 2 years' imprisonment.

132
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,440
I'm sure you can defend yourself well enough to avoid jail.

133
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:42,439
But whether you can stay a lawyer afterward...

134
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,440
is hard to say.

135
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,840
What do you want?

136
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:46,880
To be your apprentice.

137
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,400
You did all this just to be my apprentice?

138
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,280
So many lawyers graduate every year.

139
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,640
You have to follow the best master...

140
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,840
to have a "rich" future.

141
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,319
I hired someone to follow you to find out...

142
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,760
what you like and play to your interests.

143
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,560
Who knew?

144
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:02,840
I hit the jackpot!

145
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,520
Fine, I'll take you as my apprentice.

146
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,520
But you must delete all the photos.

147
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:12,800
And you can't tell anyone about this.

148
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,960
If one more person finds out,

149
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,600
I'll terminate our relationship immediately.

150
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,200
Deal.

151
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,120
If you include the hush money as well.

152
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,360
Are you blackmailing me?

153
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,280
I recorded that.

154
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,840
It's synced to the cloud. No need to grab it.

155
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:34,000
Now we can trust each other from now on.

156
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:41,040
I believe you'll be a very fine barrister.

157
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:09,880
What's wrong?

158
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,840
My father-in-law wants me to take over...

159
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,840
as the Bar Council Chairman.

160
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,040
Don't you want to?

161
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,480
I'm wondering...

162
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,600
if I need a change.

163
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,920
Maybe we'll talk after this case is over.

164
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,160
Should I stay with you?

165
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,440
Don't worry, I won't pop pills anymore.

166
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,080
I know. I just want to stay with you.

167
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,639
Did you talk to the King of Hell for me?

168
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:13,840
Yes.

169
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,240
Then how much longer can I stay?

170
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,120
Help me one more time, and I'll tell you.

171
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,040
Don't push your luck.

172
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:23,640
Just see this through to the end.

173
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,840
Help me once more, and I won't bother you again.

174
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,560
What do you want?

175
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,040
I want you to see my wife.

176
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,600
If I don't get to the bottom of this,

177
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:38,040
I won't be able to rest in peace.

178
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,400
Chung!

179
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,519
(Miu Wah, red beans grow in the southern land.)

180
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:40,719
(How many branches bloom in spring?)

181
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,359
(I hope you will gather more. They are the tokens of longing.)

182
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:45,400
(Why did you have to treat me like this? Shek Chung)

183
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,000
Red beans grow in the southern land.

184
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,360
How many branches bloom in spring?

185
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,760
I hope you will gather more.

186
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,760
They are the tokens of longing.

187
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,360
No matter where I go,

188
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,840
you are always the one I miss.

189
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,520
A woman is here to see you.

190
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,240
She says she's the Master's friend.

191
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:32,840
You're just in time. I was looking for you.

192
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,760
Where did you get this letter?

193
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,840
Didn't I tell you already?

194
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,960
Chung wrote it himself.

195
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,720
He's the one who told me to come today.

196
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,440
Tell me the truth.

197
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,200
Were you his mistress?

198
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,839
Why do you have so many of his things?

199
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,840
Stop right there. He's not my type.

200
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,560
Is Chung not good enough for you?

201
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,160
I'm not going to waste my breath.

202
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,000
You two can talk it out yourselves.

203
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,160
I'll let Chung possess me now.

204
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,560
You can tell him whatever you want.

205
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,960
Fine. Let's see what tricks you've got.

206
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,720
You wretched woman!

207
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:42,840
How can you prove you're really Chung?

208
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:46,720
You have a plum blossom mole on your left buttock.

209
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,800
You always wear bright red underwear.

210
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,560
We first met at Diamond Cabaret.

211
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:54,240
You stepped on my feet nine times!

212
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,360
Are you really Chung?

213
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,520
You still don't believe me after all that?

214
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,040
Suzie.

215
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:35,160
I'm the only one who calls you that.

216
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,200
Suzie.

217
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,600
Because we both liked Suzie Wong.

218
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,120
You awful man!

219
00:17:46,121 --> 00:17:48,720
Why did you treat me like this?

220
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:49,800
Stop it!

221
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,280
You're playing the victim now?

222
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,880
I haven't even asked you why you treated me like this!

223
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,760
I provided your food, home, and clothes.

224
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,800
I gave you everything you wanted.

225
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,600
Why were you still so insatiable?

226
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,840
I've shared a bed with you for almost 40 years.

227
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:10,280
You still have no idea why I'm angry!

228
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,960
It's because after almost 40 years,

229
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,640
I still can't see who you really are!

230
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,240
If I don't get an answer today,

231
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,120
I won't be able to rest in peace!

232
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:26,440
Do you know why you've been with me for so long,

233
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,280
yet you still don't know who I am?

234
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:31,320
It's because you never took me seriously.

235
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:33,200
You never took me seriously!

236
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:36,120
Stop it! What are you talking about?

237
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,880
When you fooled around with women outside,

238
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,880
I turned a blind eye.

239
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:42,400
Then you even brought them home!

240
00:18:42,401 --> 00:18:44,400
You simply don't respect me at all!

241
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:50,400
Your career line is really long and straight.

242
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,560
You'll soar to great heights in the future.

243
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,280
Let's see.

244
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,240
Your future husband is very handsome.

245
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:03,760
See if it fits. Do you like it?

246
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:06,800
I love it. Thank you, Chung.

247
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,840
You're doing this to me over such trivial matters?

248
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,040
I only treated her like a daughter.

249
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:16,080
You have a dirty mind!

250
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:18,720
In your eyes,

251
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,120
everything about me is trivial.

252
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,880
Because you've never valued me.

253
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,520
How have I not valued you?

254
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,240
I've been with you since I was 17.

255
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,280
You're 30 years older than me.

256
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,120
You had already been divorced three times.

257
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,280
Everyone said I was after your money.

258
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,720
Yes, I admit I was.

259
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:37,600
Because I was very poor as a child.

260
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,720
I was almost sold as a hostess.

261
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,280
So I told myself,

262
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:44,120
I told myself I had to find a man...

263
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,280
who could give me a good life.

264
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:51,560
You coveted my youth and beauty.

265
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,760
In truth, we both knew...

266
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,000
this marriage was about mutual benefit.

267
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:02,160
Pleasing and serving you every day was my job...

268
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:05,280
because I had to ensure I was your last wife.

269
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,680
But no matter how hard I tried,

270
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,400
I couldn't stop myself from aging.

271
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,280
No matter how I maintained myself,

272
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:18,040
I couldn't keep a 25-inch waist forever.

273
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,600
Compared to your nurse,

274
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:22,200
I really felt old.

275
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:26,000
You became colder and colder to me.

276
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,800
I often wondered...

277
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,440
if you would discard me once my beauty faded.

278
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,400
What would I do then?

279
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,440
I was so scared that I dreamt she became the new Mrs. Shek,

280
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,480
wearing my clothes,

281
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,160
taking my place,

282
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,480
and feeding you.

283
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:48,360
I had those dreams every few days.

284
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,240
Do you know how terrified I was?

285
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:56,000
What attracted me to you was money.

286
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:59,440
What attracted you to me was my youth and beauty.

287
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,880
But today, you still have your money,

288
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,200
while my youth and beauty...

289
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,960
are gone!

290
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,240
The less I had to offer,

291
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:16,880
the more anxious I got.

292
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,280
You know, many times,

293
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:25,080
I felt you were more like my boss than my husband.

294
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:28,960
I was constantly afraid you would fire me.

295
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:36,000
When I think about how I gave you all my youth...

296
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,680
and did everything with you in mind,

297
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:43,960
only to likely end up with nothing...

298
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:46,120
I just couldn't accept that!

299
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,880
All these years,

300
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,560
did you really see this as just a job?

301
00:21:56,240 --> 00:22:00,160
And did you really only want to leave me one dollar?

302
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:25,560
Why does it hurt so much?

303
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:32,040
What's wrong? Did you have a fight with your wife?

304
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:33,720
What?

305
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,120
I'm asking you.

306
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:37,680
Did you possess me to fight with your wife?

307
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:41,080
What?

308
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,560
Actually...

309
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:47,480
- Go on. - Now that I think about it...

310
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:51,120
Do you think we could consider...

311
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,240
if there is any chance of...

312
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,400
Go on.

313
00:22:58,480 --> 00:22:59,520
A settlement with my wife?

314
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,440
Are you messing with me?

315
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,040
I'm not messing with you. I'm serious.

316
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,840
Now that I think about it,

317
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,480
a lot of this is just a misunderstanding.

318
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,400
I've been with my wife for decades.

319
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:42,960
I can't really leave her with just one dollar.

320
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:47,600
You didn't realize this earlier,

321
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:50,440
but now that I've settled it, you do?

322
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:53,080
Do you think this is a movie? You can't just change it.

323
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:56,360
I don't know about others,

324
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:59,280
but I'm sure you can do it.

325
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:01,120
You're so capable.

326
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:04,280
You'll find a way to help me, right?

327
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:06,680
It's impossible. Your wife is going to lose.

328
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,680
How about this?

329
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:13,160
Try to persuade my son to settle with my wife.

330
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,280
My son always listens to me.

331
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:17,760
Help me talk to him.

332
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,560
This is the last time.

333
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:28,000
I promise I'll tell the King of Hell...

334
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,200
to let you stay a little longer.

335
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,600
That was the original deal.

336
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:36,240
I mean, stay even longer.

337
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:39,040
In terms of years?

338
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:41,400
Let's say years, then. No problem.

339
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:48,440
I can't take it. I need to go rest.

340
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:52,280
Just see it through to the end.

341
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:55,200
You help me, and I'll help you.

342
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,240
I'm Barrister Yau, here to see Mr. Shek.

343
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,600
Okay, please wait a moment.

344
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:26,040
Mrs. Shek, a Barrister Yau is here to see Mr. Shek.

345
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:27,680
Okay.

346
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:29,560
All right, please wait a moment.

347
00:25:33,520 --> 00:25:35,880
Ms. Yau, what brings you here?

348
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:38,400
Oh, nothing. I was just passing by.

349
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:41,040
That's very kind of you. This way, please.

350
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:44,720
It's lucky we're here packing today.

351
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:47,120
We're usually not here.

352
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:55,240
- Ms. Yau. - Go serve some tea.

353
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,400
Please have a seat.

354
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,720
Counselor Yeung told us everything.

355
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:05,320
It's all thanks to you that we found the will...

356
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,800
that my father-in-law wrote himself.

357
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:10,080
Otherwise, that woman might have actually won.

358
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:14,120
You're our savior. Thank you so much.

359
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:18,480
I'm sorry for what I said to you before.

360
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:22,280
It's nothing. Helping Chung is what matters.

361
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:25,840
Yes, I'm sure he knows in the afterlife.

362
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:27,680
He knows his last wish is finally coming true.

363
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,480
He will be so relieved.

364
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:38,600
I watched some of Chung's old interviews.

365
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,120
He was a man with strong family values.

366
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:45,520
He always said it was most important for a family to stay together...

367
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,600
and live in harmony.

368
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,720
That was indeed his catchphrase.

369
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,200
I think that is...

370
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,080
what he wants most from you.

371
00:27:00,600 --> 00:27:01,600
So...

372
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:05,760
have you considered settling with Mrs. Shek?

373
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:08,120
What did you say?

374
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,400
I mean,

375
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:11,800
you're family after all.

376
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:14,720
Have you thought about reaching a settlement with her?

377
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:17,800
You worked so hard to find evidence for us.

378
00:27:18,360 --> 00:27:19,600
Didn't you want us to win?

379
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:21,400
Why are you asking us to settle now?

380
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:25,040
Actually, I'm looking at the big picture.

381
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:28,400
I'm trying to find the best solution for you.

382
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:32,000
You're 90 percent on your way to winning this case.

383
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:35,920
But in the long run, will you be the winner?

384
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:40,720
Chung was a legendary philanthropist.

385
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,800
He was an iconic public figure.

386
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,840
Everyone respected him when he was alive.

387
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:47,880
But as soon as he's gone, his family fights over his estate,

388
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:49,760
airing all your private business in public.

389
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,439
In the future, when people search for him,

390
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:52,440
what's the first thing they will see?

391
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:53,920
"Inheritance feud."

392
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:58,120
This will greatly damage his reputation.

393
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:01,120
You don't want this to be Chung's legacy.

394
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:03,960
I know.

395
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,840
You didn't start this mess.

396
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:10,560
But you definitely have the power...

397
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,480
to set things right.

398
00:28:15,040 --> 00:28:16,920
Right now, you can act from a position of strength...

399
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:18,880
and make a magnanimous decision.

400
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:21,200
On the grounds of family and kinship,

401
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:22,640
propose a settlement with Mrs. Shek.

402
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:25,320
That way, you'll win public acclaim.

403
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:27,400
It'll only benefit your career in showbiz.

404
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:30,400
At the same time, it protects Chung's positive image.

405
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:34,280
You hold all the cards. She has no bargaining power.

406
00:28:34,560 --> 00:28:37,000
I guarantee I can get you the best deal.

407
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:40,640
Keeping the money and your dignity, that's a true victory.

408
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:44,240
Set your sights far.

409
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:46,960
A step back opens up new horizons.

410
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,360
When I was a kid,

411
00:28:58,120 --> 00:29:00,360
my classmates envied me for having a famous father.

412
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:03,320
But I didn't think it was that great.

413
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,240
Instead, I envied those...

414
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:07,320
whose parents were ordinary people.

415
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:11,279
Their moms would pack their lunches...

416
00:29:11,280 --> 00:29:12,440
and pick them up from school.

417
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:19,120
On parents' day, the whole family would meet the teacher together.

418
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:26,160
I was the only one who met the teacher accompanied by a maid.

419
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:29,280
Because my dad had to travel for work,

420
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:31,600
my mom naturally followed him.

421
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:39,640
In a given year,

422
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,040
I might see them for less than two months.

423
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:50,160
Do you know why I like building models?

424
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,760
I wanted something to keep me company.

425
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:01,080
One time, I got burned at home.

426
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:04,240
The maid took me to the hospital.

427
00:30:04,320 --> 00:30:05,880
I was watching TV at the hospital.

428
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:12,760
I saw my dad visiting a hospital in the Mainland.

429
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:15,240
At that time, I thought,

430
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:18,760
why was he visiting other people...

431
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,240
but not his own son?

432
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,200
I once asked my mom.

433
00:30:23,201 --> 00:30:25,360
I said, "Dad is at work."

434
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:27,040
"Can you stay with me?"

435
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:31,160
She said she had to work too.

436
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,120
Her job was to accompany my dad.

437
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:37,240
If she didn't, she would be fired,

438
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:40,640
and then she would see me even less.

439
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:50,400
Every New Year, you would see me on TV with them,

440
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:53,840
telling everyone how happy we were...

441
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,000
and how blissful we were.

442
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,720
Since he wanted me to, I joined the industry.

443
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:00,160
I tried my best to do...

444
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:02,760
everything he wanted me to do.

445
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:05,640
I just wanted them to notice me and love me more.

446
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:11,560
But actually, I didn't like this industry at all.

447
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:16,840
But he didn't know.

448
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,120
Because he never asked me.

449
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:25,560
I didn't know how to tell him either.

450
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:30,400
So our relationship was very distant.

451
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:32,680
What you saw on TV...

452
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,000
was all fake.

453
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:37,080
Chung was always very chauvinistic.

454
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:38,800
There were many things he couldn't say.

455
00:31:40,240 --> 00:31:41,640
But I know he really loved you.

456
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:48,280
I know he loved me. I know.

457
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:50,640
He...

458
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:54,480
let me grow up without having to worry about money.

459
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:57,080
So in his final days,

460
00:31:57,160 --> 00:31:58,760
even though I knew he had had a big fight with Mom,

461
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:02,120
I did my duty as a son to care for him.

462
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:04,440
I stayed with him until the very end.

463
00:32:07,120 --> 00:32:09,600
I thought that once Dad was gone,

464
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:12,960
Mom wouldn't have to "work" anymore,

465
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:17,480
and we would have a normal mother-son relationship.

466
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:21,800
But when she decided to sue me,

467
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:26,240
I know she only saw me as her biological family.

468
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:32,080
Money was the most important thing to her.

469
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:39,480
So I don't want to have anything to do with her anymore.

470
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:42,680
I want a clean break.

471
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:46,160
If I told you...

472
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:49,120
reconciliation was your dad's last wish,

473
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,920
would you do it for him?

474
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:03,200
I listened to him my whole life.

475
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:06,880
Now that he's gone, I really want to make my own decision for once.

476
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:11,200
Call me heartless or selfish if you want.

477
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:14,360
Anyway, I'll take this money and leave Hong Kong.

478
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:27,360
I'll spend as much time as I can with him.

479
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:34,400
I'll let him grow up in a happy environment.

480
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:53,800
(Welcome to our bank. Please enter your PIN.)

481
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:58,559
(Withdrawal)

482
00:33:58,560 --> 00:33:59,560
(Available Balance)

483
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:12,439
(Inquiries)

484
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:13,440
How can I help you?

485
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,880
I want to help my wife and my friend...

486
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:18,600
open accounts at this bank...

487
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:20,880
so they will have money to spend when they come down here.

488
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,280
We have a "Legacy of Love Plan".

489
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:25,520
The monthly management fee is only 2,000 dollars.

490
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:34,440
Give me one reason.

491
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:38,600
She's helping me with the follow-up for the case.

492
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:40,280
She needs a little more time.

493
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:41,560
Don't lie to me!

494
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:43,800
Unless you want to die again.

495
00:34:44,160 --> 00:34:46,360
No, definitely not.

496
00:34:46,680 --> 00:34:49,080
So tell me the truth now.

497
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:52,840
She has unfinished business.

498
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:55,960
I want to help her stay a bit longer.

499
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,600
It's the cycle of karma.

500
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:00,320
Her life was shortened because she did too many wicked things.

501
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:03,320
These five days are already a bonus.

502
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:06,680
It's precisely because of karma.

503
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:08,960
Spending time with Ms. Yau these past few days,

504
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:12,720
I've found that she has a kind side.

505
00:35:14,640 --> 00:35:17,120
I'm sure she wasn't born this bad.

506
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:21,079
She must have gone through something tragic...

507
00:35:21,080 --> 00:35:22,600
to become like this.

508
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:25,720
According to you,

509
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:28,960
every poor person is allowed to steal.

510
00:35:29,720 --> 00:35:30,960
Your Majesty,

511
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:33,760
there must be a reason...

512
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:36,280
you let Ms. Yau return to the living.

513
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:41,520
From your observation, can she really be saved?

514
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:44,400
Yes, absolutely.

515
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:49,600
Ms. Yau is a very smart person.

516
00:35:50,240 --> 00:35:52,600
Instead of dragging her down to rip out her tongue,

517
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:54,679
why not let her stay in the living world...

518
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:55,760
to do more good deeds?

519
00:35:57,200 --> 00:35:58,280
She can help those restless souls.

520
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:01,200
It's better than letting them become vengeful spirits.

521
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:03,840
Or how about this?

522
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:06,280
Your Majesty, you keep an eye on her yourself.

523
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:10,520
If she does anything more evil, you can take her then.

524
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:13,520
What you said makes sense.

525
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:18,280
But if I just do as you say,

526
00:36:18,640 --> 00:36:19,680
won't I lose face?

527
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:24,360
Looking at the points of contention in this case,

528
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:27,880
it lies in the validity of the late Mr. Shek Chung's will.

529
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:30,039
Given that the defendant, Shek Kwong Sing,

530
00:36:30,040 --> 00:36:31,959
provided a draft of the will...

531
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:34,440
written in Shek Chung's own handwriting,

532
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:36,760
although it has no legal force,

533
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:39,200
the contents of this draft...

534
00:36:39,640 --> 00:36:41,800
correspond to the will...

535
00:36:41,880 --> 00:36:44,000
made by Shek Chung before his death...

536
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:46,520
in the presence of two lawyers.

537
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:51,600
I believe this is enough to reflect Shek Chung's true intentions.

538
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:55,880
Shek Chung indeed intended to appoint his only son,

539
00:36:56,160 --> 00:36:57,160
Shek Kwong Sing,

540
00:36:57,400 --> 00:37:00,080
the defendant, as the estate administrator,

541
00:37:00,720 --> 00:37:03,360
and bequeathed all his assets to the defendant.

542
00:37:04,280 --> 00:37:06,400
Furthermore, the plaintiff Kwok Miu Wah's testimony...

543
00:37:06,880 --> 00:37:08,600
is clearly at odds with the objective evidence,

544
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:11,320
namely the facts presented...

545
00:37:11,840 --> 00:37:12,920
in the CCTV footage.

546
00:37:13,520 --> 00:37:15,240
I believe her purpose was...

547
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:18,640
to hide the deterioration of their marriage,

548
00:37:19,600 --> 00:37:21,160
thus denying the possibility of Shek Chung...

549
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:22,880
changing his will.

550
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,760
It is evident that the plaintiff...

551
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,960
is not an honest and reliable witness.

552
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:29,400
I refuse to accept her testimony.

553
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:34,320
I rule against the plaintiff, Kwok Miu Wah.

554
00:37:35,160 --> 00:37:38,320
Shek Kwong Sing is Shek Chung's estate administrator...

555
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:41,600
and also the legal heir to the estate.

556
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:45,080
The plaintiff must also bear the legal costs of this case.

557
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:46,960
Court is adjourned.

558
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:47,960
Court.

559
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:08,520
If I hadn't made so much money...

560
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,160
and had lived a simple life instead,

561
00:38:13,240 --> 00:38:14,240
would their relationship...

562
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:16,440
have been better?

563
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:20,480
Even if she liked you for your money,

564
00:38:20,560 --> 00:38:21,560
she still liked you.

565
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:24,440
Being poor has its own troubles.

566
00:38:25,600 --> 00:38:26,600
Trouble is trouble either way.

567
00:38:27,680 --> 00:38:28,680
I would rather be rich.

568
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,560
It's all my fault.

569
00:38:46,520 --> 00:38:48,680
If I had done a better job when I was alive,

570
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:52,400
things might not have ended up like this.

571
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:58,480
To err is human.

572
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:04,080
Cherish those around you,

573
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,200
especially your family.

574
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,040
No matter how wrong they are,

575
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:13,840
blood is thicker than water.

576
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:22,199
You haven't even sorted your own life,

577
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:23,360
yet you're lecturing me.

578
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:26,080
I'm not lecturing you.

579
00:39:27,080 --> 00:39:28,080
I'm speaking from experience.

580
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:30,880
I made mistakes.

581
00:39:32,520 --> 00:39:33,960
I don't want you to make them too.

582
00:39:36,320 --> 00:39:37,760
I've been around the block longer than you have.

583
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:40,920
Even though you haven't told me,

584
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:44,760
I can guess a few things.

585
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:58,760
Mrs. Shek, do you accept the verdict?

586
00:39:58,840 --> 00:40:00,040
Will you appeal?

587
00:40:00,120 --> 00:40:01,760
We have to leave now. Excuse us.

588
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:02,920
No comment.

589
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,800
All right, let's go have a nice meal.

590
00:40:04,880 --> 00:40:06,360
Great, I want to eat at Doco.

591
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:08,120
You brat, you only dine at expensive spots.

592
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:10,400
What? Of course we should eat something nice to celebrate.

593
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:12,040
What about you? Can you join?

594
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,200
Sorry.

595
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:21,240
Hello?

596
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:24,640
I'll be right there.

597
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:28,280
Something came up. I have to go.

598
00:40:34,600 --> 00:40:35,600
Besides you,

599
00:40:35,601 --> 00:40:37,520
who else can make her come at their beck and call?

600
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:49,800
Platinum.

601
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:52,840
Darn it! It's a gold card again.
